<p>President Donald Trump said Tuesday that Americans&#x27; financial strain is not driving his effort to reach a deal with Iran, telling reporters at the White House that his focus is preventing Tehran from obtaining a nuclear weapon. Asked how much Americans&#x27; financial situations were driving him to make a deal, Trump answered, &quot;Not even a little bit,&quot; and said, &quot;We cannot let Iran have a nuclear weapon&quot;. The remarks followed months of conflict with Iran and rising U.S. living costs tied by several reports to higher energy prices after Iran restricted access to the Strait of Hormuz, a waterway normally used for about one-fifth of global oil flows. Trump spoke as he headed to China for a summit with President Xi Jinping. He told reporters he did not think he needed China&#x27;s help to end the war with Iran, saying, &quot;We&#x27;ll win it one way or the other, peacefully or otherwise&quot;.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/cyV2SV-_HTdKBFt__BXc94yh-M638xX_XXJ9IZC78g2lWo2oEZ-_HtIHJ_i2mybFPDbj5a5EwhMaCaSRr4YjMW9pgbRMPG5PS5VkMhqLNqABtkal4hfC9CeUOC4RRasE3pS03Fkc3XrBVswzVnePw60qTFwJcAVt14_C3IzW7XGy9HSgQzaWsqApVGt4Z-4VIOgpTTJbsWTusBO7MQFXxpDPeTh_cmhs4UzTZccPlLPHOZgg07Y63gZfHnTlnSKAx2tL-G6y8L2altjLZQ' alt='U.S. President Donald Trump speaks to reporters as he departs the White House for a trip to China on May 12, 2026, in Washington.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Inflation data: Annahar reported U.S. inflation was 3.8%, the highest in three years, while Kurier reported that April U.S. consumer prices rose at their fastest pace in three years.</li><li>Diplomatic status: The Express Tribune reported that more than one month after a tenuous ceasefire took effect, the two sides had made no progress on an agreement to end hostilities.</li></ul><blockquote>The only thing that matters when I&#x27;m talking about Iran, they can&#x27;t have a nuclear weapon. I don&#x27;t think about Americans&#x27; financial situation, I don&#x27;t think about anybody. I think about one thing — we cannot let Iran have a nuclear weapon, that&#x27;s all. - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: Trump told a follow-up questioner that the stock market&#x27;s movement was secondary to preventing Iran from obtaining a nuclear weapon, adding, &quot;Every American understands.&quot; (<a href='https://www.nbcboston.com/news/politics/president-trump/trump-not-thinking-american-finances-iran-talk/3948885/'>NBC Boston</a>)</li><li>White House: Communications Director Steven Cheung defended the president&#x27;s stance by saying action was needed because a nuclear-armed Iran would threaten all Americans. (<a href='https://english.aaj.tv/news/330458880/trump-stopping-irans-nuclear-programme-outweighs-americans-economic-pain'>Aaj TV</a>)</li><li>Critics: Critics said the administration should balance geopolitical objectives with the economic impact on Americans, particularly as cost-of-living concerns remain a top issue for voters ahead of the November midterm elections. (<a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/trump-dismisses-americans-economic-pain-over-war/'>Michael West Media</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/inthenews/comments/1tbbn6l/trump_brushes_off_iran_wars_cost_at_home_i_dont/'>Trump brushes off Iran war’s cost at home: ‘I don’t think about American financial situation’</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/watch-i-dont-think-about-americans-financial-situation-when-negotiating-with-iran-trump-says'>WATCH: &#x27;I don&#x27;t think about Americans&#x27; financial situation&#x27; when negotiating with Iran, Trump says</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/trump-dismisses-americans-economic-pain-over-war/'>Trump dismisses Americans’ economic pain over war</a> - michaelwest.com.au</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-trump-iran-nuclear-us-economy/'>Stopping Iran’s nuclear pr